+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates the input received from the model against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before forwarding it to the executor, so malformed model outputs are caught at the registry boundary rather than propagated to individual tool implementations.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- When input does not satisfy the tool's `inputSchema` (missing required field, wrong type), `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing constraint, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: skips the executor and names the missing required field in its rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+
+- A `ToolResponse` rejection is returned to the calling orchestrator and fed back to the model as a tool result, so a malformed call becomes something the model can read and correct within its tool-round budget rather than ending the conversation ([validated by: resolves and makes the rejection text visible to the provider before the caller retries](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
